			'faqs' => array(array('What does an AI consultancy do?','An AI consultancy helps you decide where AI will add value, then builds and embeds it. That spans strategy and readiness, use-case prioritisation, building automation and AI agents, integrating with existing systems, governance, and training staff. Alugence delivers all of this end to end, rather than handing you a slide deck.'),array('How is Alugence different from other AI consultancies?','Alugence pairs AI adoption with AI search visibility under one brand, and delivers with named senior consultants rather than an anonymous team. We prioritise use cases by value, effort and risk, and measure outcomes — from hours saved to citations earned in AI answer engines.'),array('How much does AI consulting cost?','Fixed-fee diagnostics start from £3,500 / $4,500, pilots from £15,000 / $19,000, and production builds from £40,000 / $50,000, with monthly retainers and day rates available. See pricing for details, or try the AI ROI Calculator.'),array('Where do we start?','Most clients start with an AI Readiness Assessment or a two-week AI Readiness Sprint. It gives you a readiness score, a shortlist of prioritised use cases, and a costed plan — a low-risk way to begin. Book a discovery call to scope it.'),array('Do you work with small businesses and enterprises?','Both. We have packaged, affordable support for small businesses and a governance-led enterprise AI practice for larger organisations working with IT, security and compliance teams.')),
