		'/ai-consultancy/ai-chatbots/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>An AI chatbot for business is a conversational assistant that understands natural language and handles customer enquiries, bookings and support around the clock. Alugence builds custom AI chatbots and conversational AI grounded in your own content and tone of voice — so they answer accurately, escalate sensibly, and free your team from repetitive questions.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>Conversational AI is technology that lets people interact with software in natural language — through chat or voice — and get useful, human-like responses. Modern AI chatbots use large language models grounded in your own knowledge base, so instead of rigid menu trees they understand what\'s being asked and respond accurately. See also <a href="/ai-consultancy/voice-ai/">Voice AI</a>.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Custom chatbot build','body'=>'<p>An assistant trained on your content, policies and tone.</p>'),array('title'=>'Channel integration','body'=>'<p>Website, WhatsApp, and messaging platforms.</p>'),array('title'=>'Systems connection','body'=>'<p>Booking, CRM and helpdesk integration so it can act, not just answer.</p>'),array('title'=>'Guardrails & escalation','body'=>'<p>Accurate answers, safe boundaries, and clean handoff to humans.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Scope','desc'=>'the questions and tasks to handle.'),array('name'=>'Ground','desc'=>'the bot in your content and systems.'),array('name'=>'Build & test','desc'=>'for accuracy and safe escalation.'),array('name'=>'Deploy','desc'=>'across your channels.'),array('name'=>'Improve','desc'=>'using real conversations.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>24/7 responses to common enquiries.</li><li>Lower support load and faster answers.</li><li>More bookings and captured leads out of hours.</li><li>A chatbot that reflects your brand and gets facts right.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Businesses with high enquiry volumes or out-of-hours demand — clinics, retailers, property, professional services — that want to respond instantly without adding headcount.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('How is an AI chatbot different from an old-style chatbot?','Old chatbots follow rigid, pre-set menus and break when users go off-script. An AI chatbot uses a large language model to understand natural language and respond flexibly, grounded in your knowledge base — so it handles real, varied questions accurately instead of frustrating dead ends.'),array('Will the chatbot give accurate answers?','Yes, when it\'s built properly. We ground the chatbot in your approved content, set guardrails so it doesn\'t answer beyond its knowledge, and design clean escalation to a human for anything sensitive or uncertain. We then refine it using real conversations.'),array('Can the chatbot book appointments or update our systems?','Yes. We integrate the chatbot with your booking system, CRM or helpdesk so it can take actions — booking appointments, capturing leads, creating tickets — not just answer questions. That\'s where most of the value comes from.'),array('How long does AI chatbot development take?','A focused AI chatbot typically takes a few weeks to build, test and deploy, depending on how much content it needs to learn and how many systems it connects to. We start with the highest-value questions and expand from there.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is conversational AI?','html'=>'<p>Conversational AI is technology that lets people interact with software in natural language — through chat or voice — and get useful, human-like responses. Modern AI chatbots use large language models grounded in your own knowledge base, so instead of rigid menu trees they understand what\'s being asked and respond accurately. See also <a href="/ai-consultancy/voice-ai/">Voice AI</a>.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Custom chatbot build</h3>
<p>An assistant trained on your content, policies and tone.</p>
<h3>Channel integration</h3>
<p>Website, WhatsApp, and messaging platforms.</p>
<h3>Systems connection</h3>
<p>Booking, CRM and helpdesk integration so it can act, not just answer.</p>
<h3>Guardrails &amp; escalation</h3>
<p>Accurate answers, safe boundaries, and clean handoff to humans.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Scope</strong> the questions and tasks to handle.</li><li><strong>Ground</strong> the bot in your content and systems.</li><li><strong>Build &amp; test</strong> for accuracy and safe escalation.</li><li><strong>Deploy</strong> across your channels.</li><li><strong>Improve</strong> using real conversations.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>24/7 responses to common enquiries.</li><li>Lower support load and faster answers.</li><li>More bookings and captured leads out of hours.</li><li>A chatbot that reflects your brand and gets facts right.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Businesses with high enquiry volumes or out-of-hours demand — clinics, retailers, property, professional services — that want to respond instantly without adding headcount.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/ai-development/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Custom AI development is the design and build of bespoke AI software tailored to your business, rather than off-the-shelf tools. As an AI development company, Alugence builds custom AI solutions — from machine learning models to LLM-powered applications — and takes them from prototype to production, integrated with your systems.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>Custom AI development is building AI software designed around your specific data, workflows and goals. It spans machine learning models, LLM-based applications, and the surrounding software — APIs, interfaces and integrations — needed to use them. You get a solution that fits your business precisely, rather than bending your business to fit a generic product.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Bespoke AI applications','body'=>'<p>LLM-powered tools, internal copilots and customer-facing AI built to your requirements.</p>'),array('title'=>'Machine learning models','body'=>'<p>Custom models for prediction, classification and analysis on your data (see <a href="/ai-consultancy/predictive-analytics/">Predictive Analytics</a>).</p>'),array('title'=>'Prototype to production','body'=>'<p>Rapid prototypes to validate value, then hardened, production-grade builds.</p>'),array('title'=>'Integration & maintenance','body'=>'<p>Connection to your systems, plus ongoing support and improvement.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Define','desc'=>'the problem, data and success criteria.'),array('name'=>'Prototype','desc'=>'to prove feasibility and value.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'the production solution.'),array('name'=>'Integrate','desc'=>'and deploy.'),array('name'=>'Support','desc'=>'and improve over time.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>A bespoke AI solution that fits your workflows exactly.</li><li>Validated value before full build, via prototyping.</li><li>Production-grade software with support and documentation.</li><li>Ownership and clarity — no black boxes.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Businesses whose needs aren\'t met by off-the-shelf tools — because of specialised data, workflows, compliance requirements, or a product opportunity — and who want a partner to build it properly.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What does an AI development company do?','An AI development company designs and builds custom AI software — machine learning models, LLM applications and the integrations around them — tailored to a client\'s data and goals. Alugence covers the full lifecycle: problem definition, prototyping, production build, integration and ongoing support.'),array('Should we build custom AI or buy an off-the-shelf tool?','Buy when a proven tool already fits your need; build when your data, workflows or compliance requirements are specialised, or when the capability is a competitive advantage. We\'ll advise honestly — often the best answer is a mix, with custom development where it genuinely adds value.'),array('How much does custom AI development cost?','It depends on scope, but custom builds typically begin with a discovery and prototype phase from around £15,000 / $19,000, then a production build (from £40,000 / $50,000). We prototype first to validate value before larger spend. See pricing.'),array('What is machine learning consulting?','Machine learning consulting is expert help designing, building and deploying ML models — choosing the right approach, preparing data, training and evaluating models, and putting them into production. It\'s part of our development and predictive analytics work.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is custom AI development?','html'=>'<p>Custom AI development is building AI software designed around your specific data, workflows and goals. It spans machine learning models, LLM-based applications, and the surrounding software — APIs, interfaces and integrations — needed to use them. You get a solution that fits your business precisely, rather than bending your business to fit a generic product.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Bespoke AI applications</h3>
<p>LLM-powered tools, internal copilots and customer-facing AI built to your requirements.</p>
<h3>Machine learning models</h3>
<p>Custom models for prediction, classification and analysis on your data (see <a href="/ai-consultancy/predictive-analytics/">Predictive Analytics</a>).</p>
<h3>Prototype to production</h3>
<p>Rapid prototypes to validate value, then hardened, production-grade builds.</p>
<h3>Integration &amp; maintenance</h3>
<p>Connection to your systems, plus ongoing support and improvement.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Define</strong> the problem, data and success criteria.</li><li><strong>Prototype</strong> to prove feasibility and value.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> the production solution.</li><li><strong>Integrate</strong> and deploy.</li><li><strong>Support</strong> and improve over time.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>A bespoke AI solution that fits your workflows exactly.</li><li>Validated value before full build, via prototyping.</li><li>Production-grade software with support and documentation.</li><li>Ownership and clarity — no black boxes.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Businesses whose needs aren\'t met by off-the-shelf tools — because of specialised data, workflows, compliance requirements, or a product opportunity — and who want a partner to build it properly.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI governance is the framework of policies, controls and oversight that lets an organisation use AI safely, legally and responsibly. Alugence helps you deploy AI with confidence — mapping your regulatory perimeter under the EU AI Act and UK rules, writing practical policies, and putting controls in place that manage risk without slowing you down.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI governance is how an organisation directs and controls its use of AI so it\'s safe, compliant and aligned with its values. It covers policies for acceptable use, risk assessment of AI systems, data protection, human oversight, monitoring, and accountability. Good governance is an enabler, not a blocker — it\'s what lets you scale AI without nasty surprises.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Regulatory perimeter mapping','body'=>'<p>Where you sit under the EU AI Act, UK guidance and GDPR.</p>'),array('title'=>'AI policies & acceptable use','body'=>'<p>Clear, practical policies your teams can actually follow.</p>'),array('title'=>'Risk assessment','body'=>'<p>Classifying and assessing AI use cases by risk.</p>'),array('title'=>'Controls & human oversight','body'=>'<p>Guardrails, human-in-the-loop, logging and monitoring.</p>'),array('title'=>'Accountability','body'=>'<p>Roles, sign-off and review processes.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Map','desc'=>'your regulatory perimeter and current AI use.'),array('name'=>'Assess','desc'=>'risk across use cases.'),array('name'=>'Draft','desc'=>'policies and controls.'),array('name'=>'Embed','desc'=>'oversight, logging and monitoring.'),array('name'=>'Review','desc'=>'on an ongoing cadence.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>AI deployed safely and legally under the EU AI Act and UK rules.</li><li>Clear policies your teams understand and follow.</li><li>Risk managed proportionately — controls that fit the use case.</li><li>Board-level confidence to scale AI.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Enterprises and regulated businesses — financial services, healthcare, legal — and any organisation scaling AI that needs to prove it\'s doing so responsibly. Pairs with <a href="/ai-consultancy/enterprise-ai/">Enterprise AI</a>.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is AI governance?','AI governance is the set of policies, controls and oversight that keeps an organisation\'s use of AI safe, compliant and accountable. It includes acceptable-use policies, risk assessment, data protection, human oversight and monitoring — the framework that lets you scale AI responsibly.'),array('Does the EU AI Act apply to my business?','The EU AI Act can apply to organisations outside the EU if they offer AI systems or outputs used in the EU, and it classifies systems by risk with different obligations. We map your specific exposure and tell you what, if anything, you need to do — rather than applying a generic checklist.'),array('How does AI governance relate to GDPR?','They overlap: much AI uses personal data, so GDPR obligations around lawful basis, transparency and data protection apply alongside AI-specific rules. We align your AI governance with your existing data protection framework so they work together, not in conflict.'),array('Will governance slow down our AI adoption?','Done well, no — it speeds it up. Clear, proportionate policies let teams move confidently instead of stalling on "are we allowed to?" We right-size controls to each use case\'s risk, so low-risk work isn\'t burdened with heavy process.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI governance?','html'=>'<p>AI governance is how an organisation directs and controls its use of AI so it\'s safe, compliant and aligned with its values. It covers policies for acceptable use, risk assessment of AI systems, data protection, human oversight, monitoring, and accountability. Good governance is an enabler, not a blocker — it\'s what lets you scale AI without nasty surprises.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Regulatory perimeter mapping</h3>
<p>Where you sit under the EU AI Act, UK guidance and GDPR.</p>
<h3>AI policies &amp; acceptable use</h3>
<p>Clear, practical policies your teams can actually follow.</p>
<h3>Risk assessment</h3>
<p>Classifying and assessing AI use cases by risk.</p>
<h3>Controls &amp; human oversight</h3>
<p>Guardrails, human-in-the-loop, logging and monitoring.</p>
<h3>Accountability</h3>
<p>Roles, sign-off and review processes.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Map</strong> your regulatory perimeter and current AI use.</li><li><strong>Assess</strong> risk across use cases.</li><li><strong>Draft</strong> policies and controls.</li><li><strong>Embed</strong> oversight, logging and monitoring.</li><li><strong>Review</strong> on an ongoing cadence.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>AI deployed safely and legally under the EU AI Act and UK rules.</li><li>Clear policies your teams understand and follow.</li><li>Risk managed proportionately — controls that fit the use case.</li><li>Board-level confidence to scale AI.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Enterprises and regulated businesses — financial services, healthcare, legal — and any organisation scaling AI that needs to prove it\'s doing so responsibly. Pairs with <a href="/ai-consultancy/enterprise-ai/">Enterprise AI</a>.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/ai-implementation/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI implementation is the work of building, deploying and integrating AI into your existing systems so it delivers value in production — not just in a demo. Alugence takes proven use cases and embeds them safely into your stack, with the security, monitoring and documentation to run them reliably at scale.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI implementation is the end-to-end process of turning an AI use case into a working, integrated system. It covers solution design, building or configuring the models, connecting to your data and applications, deploying to production, and setting up monitoring and support. Integration — making AI work with your CRM, ERP, data warehouse and workflows — is where most projects succeed or stall.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Solution design','body'=>'<p>An architecture that fits your systems, data and security posture.</p>'),array('title'=>'Build & configuration','body'=>'<p>Building the AI system or configuring off-the-shelf models to your needs.</p>'),array('title'=>'Systems integration','body'=>'<p>Connecting AI to your existing stack — CRM, ERP, ticketing, data warehouse — via APIs and secure data flows.</p>'),array('title'=>'Deployment & monitoring','body'=>'<p>Production deployment with observability, alerting and cost controls (see <a href="/ai-consultancy/mlops/">MLOps</a>).</p>'),array('title'=>'Handover','body'=>'<p>Documentation, runbooks and training so your team can operate it.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Design','desc'=>'the solution and integration architecture.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'or configure the AI system.'),array('name'=>'Integrate','desc'=>'with your existing applications and data.'),array('name'=>'Deploy','desc'=>'to production with security and monitoring.'),array('name'=>'Handover','desc'=>'with documentation and training.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>AI running in production and integrated with your real systems.</li><li>A secure, monitored deployment with cost controls.</li><li>Documentation and runbooks for reliable operation.</li><li>A repeatable pattern you can extend to the next use case.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Organisations that have validated a use case (often via a <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-proof-of-concept/">pilot</a>) and need it built and embedded properly — including enterprises working with IT, security and compliance teams. See <a href="/ai-consultancy/enterprise-ai/">Enterprise AI</a>.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('How long does AI implementation take?','Most production implementations take 8–16 weeks, depending on integration complexity and your data readiness. Simpler deployments are faster; heavily integrated, enterprise-grade builds take longer. We scope the timeline precisely after a discovery phase or pilot.'),array('Can you integrate AI with our existing systems?','Yes. Integration is core to what we do — connecting AI to CRMs, ERPs, data warehouses, ticketing and bespoke applications through secure APIs and data pipelines. We design the integration around your security and compliance requirements from the start.'),array('Do we need a pilot before full implementation?','Not always, but a pilot de-risks bigger builds by proving value on your real data first. If the use case is well understood and low-risk, we can proceed straight to implementation. See AI Proof of Concept & Pilots.'),array('How do you keep AI deployments secure and compliant?','We build security and governance in from design — data handling, access controls, and alignment with GDPR and the EU AI Act. For ongoing controls and monitoring see AI Governance and MLOps.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI implementation?','html'=>'<p>AI implementation is the end-to-end process of turning an AI use case into a working, integrated system. It covers solution design, building or configuring the models, connecting to your data and applications, deploying to production, and setting up monitoring and support. Integration — making AI work with your CRM, ERP, data warehouse and workflows — is where most projects succeed or stall.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Solution design</h3>
<p>An architecture that fits your systems, data and security posture.</p>
<h3>Build &amp; configuration</h3>
<p>Building the AI system or configuring off-the-shelf models to your needs.</p>
<h3>Systems integration</h3>
<p>Connecting AI to your existing stack — CRM, ERP, ticketing, data warehouse — via APIs and secure data flows.</p>
<h3>Deployment &amp; monitoring</h3>
<p>Production deployment with observability, alerting and cost controls (see <a href="/ai-consultancy/mlops/">MLOps</a>).</p>
<h3>Handover</h3>
<p>Documentation, runbooks and training so your team can operate it.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Design</strong> the solution and integration architecture.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> or configure the AI system.</li><li><strong>Integrate</strong> with your existing applications and data.</li><li><strong>Deploy</strong> to production with security and monitoring.</li><li><strong>Handover</strong> with documentation and training.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>AI running in production and integrated with your real systems.</li><li>A secure, monitored deployment with cost controls.</li><li>Documentation and runbooks for reliable operation.</li><li>A repeatable pattern you can extend to the next use case.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Organisations that have validated a use case (often via a <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-proof-of-concept/">pilot</a>) and need it built and embedded properly — including enterprises working with IT, security and compliance teams. See <a href="/ai-consultancy/enterprise-ai/">Enterprise AI</a>.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/ai-proof-of-concept/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>An AI proof of concept (PoC) is a fast, fixed-scope build that tests whether an AI use case works on your real data before you invest in full development. Alugence runs AI PoCs and pilots that prove — or disprove — value in weeks, so you make your bigger AI decisions on evidence, not hope.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>An AI proof of concept is a small, time-boxed project that validates a specific AI use case using your actual data and workflows. It answers a clear question — will this work, and is it worth building? — with a working prototype and evidence, before you spend on production. A pilot goes a step further, running the solution with real users on a limited scale.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Fixed scope & question','body'=>'<p>One clear use case and success criteria.</p>'),array('title'=>'Working prototype','body'=>'<p>Built on your real (or representative) data.</p>'),array('title'=>'Evidence & recommendation','body'=>'<p>Results, limitations, and a clear build-or-stop recommendation.</p>'),array('title'=>'Path to production','body'=>'<p>If it works, a costed plan to scale (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-implementation/">implementation</a>).</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Define','desc'=>'the use case, data and success criteria.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'a working prototype fast.'),array('name'=>'Test','desc'=>'against real cases and measure results.'),array('name'=>'Decide','desc'=>'— a clear go/no-go with evidence.'),array('name'=>'Plan','desc'=>'production if validated.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Evidence-based confidence before a big commitment.</li><li>A working prototype in weeks, not months.</li><li>Lower risk — you find the dead ends cheaply.</li><li>A costed route to production for what works.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Businesses weighing a significant AI investment who want proof first, and teams that need to win internal buy-in with a tangible result.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is the difference between a proof of concept and a pilot?','A proof of concept tests whether an AI use case *can* work, usually as a prototype in a controlled setting; a pilot tests whether it *does* work in practice, running with real users at limited scale. PoC comes first to validate feasibility; a pilot validates real-world fit before full rollout.'),array('How long does an AI proof of concept take?','Most AI PoCs run in four to eight weeks, depending on data access and complexity. The point is speed — a time-boxed build that gives you a clear answer quickly. Our AI Discovery & Pilot package starts from £15,000 / $19,000; see pricing.'),array('Why not just build the full solution?','Because full builds are expensive and not every idea survives contact with real data. A PoC finds the problems cheaply and proves value before you commit, dramatically reducing the risk of a costly build that doesn\'t deliver.'),array('What happens if the PoC doesn\'t work?','That\'s still a valuable outcome — you\'ve avoided a much larger wasted investment, and you\'ll know exactly why it didn\'t work and what would need to change. Often we learn enough to pivot to a better-scoped use case.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is an AI proof of concept?','html'=>'<p>An AI proof of concept is a small, time-boxed project that validates a specific AI use case using your actual data and workflows. It answers a clear question — will this work, and is it worth building? — with a working prototype and evidence, before you spend on production. A pilot goes a step further, running the solution with real users on a limited scale.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Fixed scope &amp; question</h3>
<p>One clear use case and success criteria.</p>
<h3>Working prototype</h3>
<p>Built on your real (or representative) data.</p>
<h3>Evidence &amp; recommendation</h3>
<p>Results, limitations, and a clear build-or-stop recommendation.</p>
<h3>Path to production</h3>
<p>If it works, a costed plan to scale (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-implementation/">implementation</a>).</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Define</strong> the use case, data and success criteria.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> a working prototype fast.</li><li><strong>Test</strong> against real cases and measure results.</li><li><strong>Decide</strong> — a clear go/no-go with evidence.</li><li><strong>Plan</strong> production if validated.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Evidence-based confidence before a big commitment.</li><li>A working prototype in weeks, not months.</li><li>Lower risk — you find the dead ends cheaply.</li><li>A costed route to production for what works.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Businesses weighing a significant AI investment who want proof first, and teams that need to win internal buy-in with a tangible result.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/ai-readiness/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>An AI readiness assessment is a structured evaluation of how prepared your business is to adopt AI — across your data, tools, team and processes. Alugence\'s assessment gives you a clear readiness score, tells you what to fix first, and produces a prioritised, costed shortlist of use cases, so your first AI investment is a safe bet rather than a gamble.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>An AI readiness assessment measures an organisation\'s ability to adopt AI successfully and identifies the gaps to close first. It typically scores four dimensions — data, tooling, team capability, and momentum — and maps candidate use cases against value, effort and risk. The result is a clear picture of where you stand and what to do next, before you commit budget.</p>',
			'cards' => array(),
			'steps' => array(),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Confidence about whether — and where — to invest in AI.</li><li>A de-risked first project with the highest chance of payback.</li><li>A shared, evidence-based view across your leadership team.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Any organisation considering AI that wants to invest wisely — first-time adopters especially, and anyone whose earlier AI efforts stalled.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is an AI readiness assessment?','It\'s a structured evaluation of how ready your business is to adopt AI, scoring your data, tools, team and momentum, and identifying the gaps to close. It ends with a prioritised, costed shortlist of use cases so you invest where payback is most likely.'),array('How long does it take?','A focused AI readiness assessment typically runs over one to two weeks. Our two-week AI Readiness Sprint packages it with a data and process audit, regulatory check and written report. See pricing.'),array('How is this different from the free AI ROI Calculator?','The AI ROI Calculator gives an instant, indicative readiness score and savings estimate from a few inputs. The full assessment is a consultant-led deep dive into your actual data, tools and processes, producing a validated plan you can act on.'),array('What if we\'re not ready?','That\'s a useful result. The assessment tells you exactly what to shore up first — often data or tooling — so you don\'t waste money on AI that can\'t succeed yet. We\'ll sequence those foundations alongside any low-risk quick wins.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is an AI readiness assessment?','html'=>'<p>An AI readiness assessment measures an organisation\'s ability to adopt AI successfully and identifies the gaps to close first. It typically scores four dimensions — data, tooling, team capability, and momentum — and maps candidate use cases against value, effort and risk. The result is a clear picture of where you stand and what to do next, before you commit budget.</p>'),array('h'=>'What we assess','html'=>'<h3>Data</h3>
<p>Where your data lives, its quality, and whether it\'s usable for AI.</p>
<h3>Tooling</h3>
<p>Your current systems and how AI-ready they are.</p>
<h3>Team</h3>
<p>Skills, confidence and capacity to adopt AI.</p>
<h3>Momentum</h3>
<p>Past attempts, leadership appetite and change readiness.</p>'),array('h'=>'What you get','html'=>'<ol><li>A <strong>readiness score</strong> with a clear band (foundations first / ready to pilot / ready to scale).</li><li>A <strong>gap analysis</strong> — what to fix first.</li><li>A <strong>prioritised use-case shortlist</strong> scored on value, effort and risk.</li><li>A <strong>costed next step</strong> — usually a pilot or quick win.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Confidence about whether — and where — to invest in AI.</li><li>A de-risked first project with the highest chance of payback.</li><li>A shared, evidence-based view across your leadership team.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Any organisation considering AI that wants to invest wisely — first-time adopters especially, and anyone whose earlier AI efforts stalled.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/ai-strategy/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI strategy consulting helps you decide where AI will create the most value, then plan how to get there. Alugence builds a clear, costed AI roadmap: we assess your readiness, prioritise use cases by value, effort and risk, and give you a sequenced plan your leadership team can back with confidence.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI strategy consulting is advisory work that turns a broad ambition to "use AI" into a concrete, prioritised plan. It defines where AI fits your goals, which use cases to pursue first, what data and governance you need, and how to measure return. The output is an AI roadmap — not a slide deck, but a costed sequence of steps you can execute.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'AI readiness assessment','body'=>'<p>We evaluate your data, tools, team and processes to see how ready you are, and what to fix first. See <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-readiness/">AI Readiness Assessment</a>.</p>'),array('title'=>'Use-case discovery & prioritisation','body'=>'<p>We identify candidate use cases across your business and score each on value, effort and risk, so you invest where payback is fastest.</p>'),array('title'=>'AI roadmap','body'=>'<p>A sequenced, costed plan — quick wins first, foundations in parallel, bigger bets staged — with owners and success metrics.</p>'),array('title'=>'Transformation leadership','body'=>'<p>Optional ongoing leadership to drive delivery, via a <a href="/ai-consultancy/fractional-ai-officer/">Fractional CAIO</a>.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Discover','desc'=>'— understand your goals, constraints and current state.'),array('name'=>'Assess','desc'=>'— score readiness across data, tooling, team and momentum.'),array('name'=>'Prioritise','desc'=>'— rank use cases on value/effort/risk.'),array('name'=>'Roadmap','desc'=>'— produce a costed, sequenced plan with metrics.'),array('name'=>'Enable','desc'=>'— support delivery and track ROI.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>A prioritised shortlist of AI use cases with expected value.</li><li>A costed, board-ready AI roadmap and business case.</li><li>Clear governance and data prerequisites, so delivery doesn\'t stall.</li><li>A realistic view of payback — typically 6–12 months for efficiency use cases.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Leaders who know AI matters but need a defensible plan — SMEs and mid-market organisations starting out, and larger businesses aligning multiple teams behind one roadmap.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is the difference between AI strategy and AI implementation?','AI strategy decides *what* to do and in what order; AI implementation *builds and integrates* it. Strategy produces a prioritised, costed roadmap; implementation turns the top items into working systems. Alugence does both, so your plan doesn\'t sit on a shelf — see AI Implementation.'),array('How long does an AI strategy engagement take?','A focused AI strategy and roadmap typically takes two to four weeks, depending on the size of the business and number of use cases. Our two-week AI Readiness Sprint is the most common starting point and produces a scored use-case shortlist and written plan.'),array('What is an AI roadmap?','An AI roadmap is a sequenced, costed plan for adopting AI — which use cases to pursue, in what order, with what data, governance and resources, and how success is measured. It turns a general ambition into an executable programme leadership can fund and track.'),array('Do we need our data in order first?','Not necessarily to start, but data readiness shapes what\'s feasible early. Our assessment flags gaps and we sequence foundational data work alongside quick wins so momentum isn\'t lost. See AI Data Strategy.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI strategy consulting?','html'=>'<p>AI strategy consulting is advisory work that turns a broad ambition to "use AI" into a concrete, prioritised plan. It defines where AI fits your goals, which use cases to pursue first, what data and governance you need, and how to measure return. The output is an AI roadmap — not a slide deck, but a costed sequence of steps you can execute.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>AI readiness assessment</h3>
<p>We evaluate your data, tools, team and processes to see how ready you are, and what to fix first. See <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-readiness/">AI Readiness Assessment</a>.</p>
<h3>Use-case discovery &amp; prioritisation</h3>
<p>We identify candidate use cases across your business and score each on value, effort and risk, so you invest where payback is fastest.</p>
<h3>AI roadmap</h3>
<p>A sequenced, costed plan — quick wins first, foundations in parallel, bigger bets staged — with owners and success metrics.</p>
<h3>Transformation leadership</h3>
<p>Optional ongoing leadership to drive delivery, via a <a href="/ai-consultancy/fractional-ai-officer/">Fractional CAIO</a>.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Discover</strong> — understand your goals, constraints and current state.</li><li><strong>Assess</strong> — score readiness across data, tooling, team and momentum.</li><li><strong>Prioritise</strong> — rank use cases on value/effort/risk.</li><li><strong>Roadmap</strong> — produce a costed, sequenced plan with metrics.</li><li><strong>Enable</strong> — support delivery and track ROI.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>A prioritised shortlist of AI use cases with expected value.</li><li>A costed, board-ready AI roadmap and business case.</li><li>Clear governance and data prerequisites, so delivery doesn\'t stall.</li><li>A realistic view of payback — typically 6–12 months for efficiency use cases.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Leaders who know AI matters but need a defensible plan — SMEs and mid-market organisations starting out, and larger businesses aligning multiple teams behind one roadmap.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/ai-training/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI training for business is hands-on upskilling that helps your teams use AI tools confidently, safely and productively. Alugence runs practical workshops, builds playbooks, and provides ongoing enablement so AI adoption actually sticks — turning new tools into new habits and measurable productivity.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI training and enablement is the practice of building an organisation\'s AI skills and confidence so people use AI tools well. It goes beyond a one-off course: it combines role-specific training, practical playbooks, guardrails, and support that embeds AI into everyday work. Enablement is what turns a licence into adoption.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Role-based workshops','body'=>'<p>Practical, hands-on sessions tailored to each team\'s real tasks.</p>'),array('title'=>'Playbooks & prompt libraries','body'=>'<p>Reusable guides and prompts for the workflows that matter to you.</p>'),array('title'=>'Adoption support','body'=>'<p>Office hours, champions programmes and follow-up to embed new habits.</p>'),array('title'=>'Safe-use guidance','body'=>'<p>Clear policies on what\'s appropriate, aligned with your <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">governance</a>.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Assess','desc'=>'current AI literacy and priority workflows.'),array('name'=>'Design','desc'=>'role-based training and playbooks.'),array('name'=>'Deliver','desc'=>'hands-on workshops.'),array('name'=>'Embed','desc'=>'with support, champions and office hours.'),array('name'=>'Measure','desc'=>'adoption and productivity.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Teams confident and productive with AI tools.</li><li>Adoption that sticks, not a spike that fades.</li><li>Consistent, safe use guided by clear policies.</li><li>A measurable lift in day-to-day productivity.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Any organisation rolling out AI tools — from a <a href="/ai-consultancy/llm-deployment/">Claude or ChatGPT deployment</a> to bespoke systems — that wants staff to actually use them well.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('Why do AI tools fail to get adopted?','AI tools most often fail on adoption, not technology — people don\'t know how to apply them to their real work, or aren\'t confident it\'s safe. Role-based training, practical playbooks and ongoing support fix this by connecting the tools to everyday tasks and giving people clear guardrails.'),array('What does AI training for business cover?','It covers practical, role-specific use of AI tools: effective prompting, applying AI to real workflows, checking outputs, and safe-use policies. We tailor content to each team — for example, drafting and research for professional services, or support triage for customer teams.'),array('Do you offer ongoing enablement or just one-off workshops?','Both. Many clients start with workshops and add ongoing enablement — office hours, a champions programme and refreshed playbooks — because adoption embeds over months, not a single day. We measure adoption so you can see the return.'),array('Can training be tailored to our tools and sector?','Yes. We build training around the specific tools you use and the workflows of your sector, using your own examples where possible, so it\'s immediately applicable rather than generic.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI training and enablement?','html'=>'<p>AI training and enablement is the practice of building an organisation\'s AI skills and confidence so people use AI tools well. It goes beyond a one-off course: it combines role-specific training, practical playbooks, guardrails, and support that embeds AI into everyday work. Enablement is what turns a licence into adoption.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Role-based workshops</h3>
<p>Practical, hands-on sessions tailored to each team\'s real tasks.</p>
<h3>Playbooks &amp; prompt libraries</h3>
<p>Reusable guides and prompts for the workflows that matter to you.</p>
<h3>Adoption support</h3>
<p>Office hours, champions programmes and follow-up to embed new habits.</p>
<h3>Safe-use guidance</h3>
<p>Clear policies on what\'s appropriate, aligned with your <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">governance</a>.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Assess</strong> current AI literacy and priority workflows.</li><li><strong>Design</strong> role-based training and playbooks.</li><li><strong>Deliver</strong> hands-on workshops.</li><li><strong>Embed</strong> with support, champions and office hours.</li><li><strong>Measure</strong> adoption and productivity.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Teams confident and productive with AI tools.</li><li>Adoption that sticks, not a spike that fades.</li><li>Consistent, safe use guided by clear policies.</li><li>A measurable lift in day-to-day productivity.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Any organisation rolling out AI tools — from a <a href="/ai-consultancy/llm-deployment/">Claude or ChatGPT deployment</a> to bespoke systems — that wants staff to actually use them well.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/data-strategy/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI data strategy is the plan for getting your data clean, connected, compliant and usable — because AI is only ever as good as the data behind it. Alugence gets your data foundations right through data strategy, governance, migration and structuring, so your AI projects have the fuel they need instead of stalling on messy data.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI data strategy is the practice of organising an business\'s data so it can power AI reliably and compliantly. It covers what data you have and need, where it lives, its quality and structure, how it\'s governed and protected, and how it flows to AI systems. It\'s the foundation most AI projects underestimate — and the reason many stall.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Data audit & strategy','body'=>'<p>What data you have, its quality, and a plan to make it AI-ready.</p>'),array('title'=>'Data governance','body'=>'<p>Ownership, quality standards, access and compliance (GDPR-aligned).</p>'),array('title'=>'Migration & consolidation','body'=>'<p>Moving and unifying data from legacy systems and silos.</p>'),array('title'=>'Structuring & digitisation','body'=>'<p>Turning paper, spreadsheets and unstructured data into usable form.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Audit','desc'=>'your data sources, quality and structure.'),array('name'=>'Strategise','desc'=>'a plan to make data AI-ready.'),array('name'=>'Govern','desc'=>'— standards, ownership and compliance.'),array('name'=>'Migrate & structure','desc'=>'as needed.'),array('name'=>'Connect','desc'=>'data to AI systems.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Clean, connected, compliant data ready for AI.</li><li>Fewer stalled projects caused by data problems.</li><li>Clear governance and ownership.</li><li>A foundation that pays off across every future use case.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Organisations whose data is siloed, messy, or partly on paper, and anyone whose <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-readiness/">AI readiness assessment</a> flagged data as the thing to fix first.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('Why does AI need a data strategy?','Because AI is only as good as its data. Models trained or grounded on incomplete, inconsistent or inaccessible data produce poor results. A data strategy ensures your data is clean, connected, compliant and usable — the single biggest factor in whether AI projects succeed.'),array('What is data governance?','Data governance is the framework of ownership, standards, access controls and compliance that keeps data accurate, secure and used appropriately. For AI, good governance means models draw on trustworthy, permissioned data — and that you can meet obligations like GDPR.'),array('Our data is a mess — where do we start?','Start with an audit to see what you have, its quality and where it lives, then prioritise the data that your highest-value AI use cases depend on. You rarely need to fix everything at once — we sequence data work so it unblocks quick wins first.'),array('Can you help move data off legacy or paper systems?','Yes. We handle data migration, consolidation from silos, and structuring or digitising paper and unstructured data into usable form, so it can feed your AI systems reliably and compliantly.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI data strategy?','html'=>'<p>AI data strategy is the practice of organising an business\'s data so it can power AI reliably and compliantly. It covers what data you have and need, where it lives, its quality and structure, how it\'s governed and protected, and how it flows to AI systems. It\'s the foundation most AI projects underestimate — and the reason many stall.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Data audit &amp; strategy</h3>
<p>What data you have, its quality, and a plan to make it AI-ready.</p>
<h3>Data governance</h3>
<p>Ownership, quality standards, access and compliance (GDPR-aligned).</p>
<h3>Migration &amp; consolidation</h3>
<p>Moving and unifying data from legacy systems and silos.</p>
<h3>Structuring &amp; digitisation</h3>
<p>Turning paper, spreadsheets and unstructured data into usable form.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Audit</strong> your data sources, quality and structure.</li><li><strong>Strategise</strong> a plan to make data AI-ready.</li><li><strong>Govern</strong> — standards, ownership and compliance.</li><li><strong>Migrate &amp; structure</strong> as needed.</li><li><strong>Connect</strong> data to AI systems.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Clean, connected, compliant data ready for AI.</li><li>Fewer stalled projects caused by data problems.</li><li>Clear governance and ownership.</li><li>A foundation that pays off across every future use case.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Organisations whose data is siloed, messy, or partly on paper, and anyone whose <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-readiness/">AI readiness assessment</a> flagged data as the thing to fix first.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/enterprise-ai/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Enterprise AI is the strategy, governance and delivery of artificial intelligence at scale across a large organisation — safely, securely and in step with IT, security and compliance. Alugence helps enterprises move from scattered pilots to a coordinated AI programme, with the governance and integration that larger businesses require.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>Enterprise AI is the adoption of AI across a large organisation in a coordinated, governed way — as opposed to isolated departmental experiments. It combines strategy, platform and data foundations, security and compliance, integration with core systems, and change management, so AI scales reliably and safely across the business.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Enterprise AI strategy','body'=>'<p>A coordinated roadmap across functions, not siloed pilots.</p>'),array('title'=>'Governance at scale','body'=>'<p>Policies, risk management and compliance (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">AI governance</a>).</p>'),array('title'=>'Secure integration','body'=>'<p>Working with IT and security to integrate AI with core systems.</p>'),array('title'=>'Platform & MLOps','body'=>'<p>Reliable infrastructure to run AI in production (<a href="/ai-consultancy/mlops/">MLOps</a>).</p>'),array('title'=>'Change & enablement','body'=>'<p>Bringing teams with you (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-training/">AI training</a>).</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Align','desc'=>'leadership on an enterprise AI strategy.'),array('name'=>'Establish','desc'=>'governance, security and data foundations.'),array('name'=>'Prioritise','desc'=>'and sequence use cases across functions.'),array('name'=>'Deliver','desc'=>'integrated, production-grade solutions.'),array('name'=>'Scale','desc'=>'with enablement and ongoing oversight.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>A coordinated AI programme instead of scattered pilots.</li><li>Governance and security that satisfy the enterprise.</li><li>AI integrated with core systems at scale.</li><li>Faster, safer value across multiple functions.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Larger organisations with existing IT, security and compliance functions that need AI delivered at scale, safely, and in a way that survives audit and board scrutiny.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What makes enterprise AI different from other AI projects?','Enterprise AI operates at scale and across functions, so governance, security, integration with core systems, and change management matter as much as the models themselves. The challenge is less "can it work?" and more "can it work safely, repeatably and in step with IT and compliance across the whole business?"'),array('How do you work with our IT and security teams?','We work as a partner to your internal teams, aligning to your security standards, architecture and change processes from the start. Governance and security are designed in, not bolted on, so deployments pass review rather than getting blocked.'),array('How do we move from pilots to scaled AI?','By establishing shared foundations — strategy, governance, data and platform — then sequencing use cases so each builds reusable capability. We turn one-off pilots into a repeatable pattern, with the MLOps and governance to run them dependably.'),array('Is our data secure with enterprise AI?','Security is central to how we deliver: appropriate model and licensing choices, access controls, data-handling policies, and alignment with your existing security posture and GDPR obligations. We design controls proportionate to each use case\'s risk.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is enterprise AI?','html'=>'<p>Enterprise AI is the adoption of AI across a large organisation in a coordinated, governed way — as opposed to isolated departmental experiments. It combines strategy, platform and data foundations, security and compliance, integration with core systems, and change management, so AI scales reliably and safely across the business.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Enterprise AI strategy</h3>
<p>A coordinated roadmap across functions, not siloed pilots.</p>
<h3>Governance at scale</h3>
<p>Policies, risk management and compliance (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">AI governance</a>).</p>
<h3>Secure integration</h3>
<p>Working with IT and security to integrate AI with core systems.</p>
<h3>Platform &amp; MLOps</h3>
<p>Reliable infrastructure to run AI in production (<a href="/ai-consultancy/mlops/">MLOps</a>).</p>
<h3>Change &amp; enablement</h3>
<p>Bringing teams with you (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-training/">AI training</a>).</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Align</strong> leadership on an enterprise AI strategy.</li><li><strong>Establish</strong> governance, security and data foundations.</li><li><strong>Prioritise</strong> and sequence use cases across functions.</li><li><strong>Deliver</strong> integrated, production-grade solutions.</li><li><strong>Scale</strong> with enablement and ongoing oversight.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>A coordinated AI programme instead of scattered pilots.</li><li>Governance and security that satisfy the enterprise.</li><li>AI integrated with core systems at scale.</li><li>Faster, safer value across multiple functions.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Larger organisations with existing IT, security and compliance functions that need AI delivered at scale, safely, and in a way that survives audit and board scrutiny.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/fractional-ai-officer/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>A Fractional Chief AI Officer is a senior AI leader who works with your business part-time, giving you executive-level AI strategy, governance and delivery oversight without the cost of a full-time hire. Alugence provides a Fractional CAIO — typically two to four days a month — to own your AI roadmap and make sure AI investment turns into results.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>A Fractional Chief AI Officer (CAIO) is an experienced AI executive engaged on a part-time, ongoing basis to lead an organisation\'s AI agenda. They set strategy, choose vendors and tools, own the roadmap, oversee delivery and governance, and report to the board — the role a full-time CAIO would play, sized and priced for organisations that don\'t yet need a permanent hire.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Strategy & roadmap ownership','body'=>'<p>We own and drive your AI roadmap, keeping it aligned to business goals.</p>'),array('title'=>'Governance & risk','body'=>'<p>Policies, controls and compliance with the EU AI Act and UK rules (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">AI governance</a>).</p>'),array('title'=>'Vendor & tool selection','body'=>'<p>Independent advice on what to buy, build or avoid.</p>'),array('title'=>'Delivery oversight','body'=>'<p>Keeping projects on track and value on the table.</p>'),array('title'=>'Board reporting','body'=>'<p>Clear updates leadership can act on.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Executive AI leadership at a fraction of a full-time salary.</li><li>A roadmap that\'s owned and actually delivered.</li><li>Governance and risk handled properly.</li><li>Better buying decisions and less wasted spend.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>SMEs and mid-market organisations that need senior AI direction but can\'t justify a full-time CAIO — and larger firms wanting experienced leadership to kick-start their AI programme.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What does a Fractional Chief AI Officer do?','A Fractional CAIO leads your AI agenda part-time: setting strategy, owning the roadmap, selecting vendors and tools, overseeing delivery, managing governance and risk, and reporting to the board. It\'s senior AI leadership on a rolling basis, without a permanent executive hire.'),array('How is a Fractional CAIO different from AI consulting?','Project consulting delivers a specific outcome and ends; a Fractional CAIO is ongoing leadership that owns your AI direction over time. Many clients use both — a Fractional CAIO to steer the programme, with project teams delivering underneath.'),array('How much does a Fractional CAIO cost?','Alugence\'s Fractional CAIO starts from £3,000 / $3,800 per month for a typical 2–4 days, on a rolling basis. It\'s a fraction of a full-time CAIO salary. See pricing for details.'),array('How many days a month do you work?','Usually two to four days a month, flexed up during key initiatives such as a major rollout or board planning cycle. We agree the rhythm with you and adjust as your programme evolves.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is a Fractional Chief AI Officer?','html'=>'<p>A Fractional Chief AI Officer (CAIO) is an experienced AI executive engaged on a part-time, ongoing basis to lead an organisation\'s AI agenda. They set strategy, choose vendors and tools, own the roadmap, oversee delivery and governance, and report to the board — the role a full-time CAIO would play, sized and priced for organisations that don\'t yet need a permanent hire.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Strategy &amp; roadmap ownership</h3>
<p>We own and drive your AI roadmap, keeping it aligned to business goals.</p>
<h3>Governance &amp; risk</h3>
<p>Policies, controls and compliance with the EU AI Act and UK rules (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">AI governance</a>).</p>
<h3>Vendor &amp; tool selection</h3>
<p>Independent advice on what to buy, build or avoid.</p>
<h3>Delivery oversight</h3>
<p>Keeping projects on track and value on the table.</p>
<h3>Board reporting</h3>
<p>Clear updates leadership can act on.</p>'),array('h'=>'How it works','html'=>'<p>Typically 2–4 days per month on a rolling basis. You get a named senior leader who knows your business, attends the meetings that matter, and drives momentum between them — flexible to scale up during key initiatives.</p>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Executive AI leadership at a fraction of a full-time salary.</li><li>A roadmap that\'s owned and actually delivered.</li><li>Governance and risk handled properly.</li><li>Better buying decisions and less wasted spend.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>SMEs and mid-market organisations that need senior AI direction but can\'t justify a full-time CAIO — and larger firms wanting experienced leadership to kick-start their AI programme.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/llm-deployment/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>LLM deployment is the managed rollout of large language models — like Claude and ChatGPT — across your organisation, done safely and usefully. Alugence handles the whole thing: licences, setup, custom GPTs and assistants built on your data, guardrails, and the training that turns a subscription into real productivity.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>LLM deployment is the process of introducing large language models into a business so teams can use them securely and effectively. It covers choosing the right models and licences, configuring them, building custom GPTs or assistants grounded in your own knowledge, setting data and safety guardrails, and training staff. The goal is safe, widespread, productive use — not scattered, risky personal accounts.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Model & licence selection','body'=>'<p>The right LLMs (Claude, ChatGPT and others) and licences for your needs.</p>'),array('title'=>'Custom GPTs & assistants','body'=>'<p>Assistants built on your data and tone of voice for real workflows.</p>'),array('title'=>'Guardrails & data safety','body'=>'<p>Controls over what data goes where, aligned with your <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">governance</a>.</p>'),array('title'=>'Rollout & training','body'=>'<p>Structured rollout with hands-on <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-training/">training</a> so adoption sticks.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Assess','desc'=>'use cases, licences and data-safety needs.'),array('name'=>'Configure','desc'=>'models and build custom GPTs/assistants.'),array('name'=>'Guardrail','desc'=>'— set data and safety controls.'),array('name'=>'Roll out','desc'=>'across teams.'),array('name'=>'Train & embed','desc'=>'for lasting adoption.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>LLMs live across your teams, used safely and well.</li><li>Custom assistants grounded in your own knowledge.</li><li>Data risk controlled, not left to chance.</li><li>Measurable productivity, not shelfware.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Organisations rolling out Claude, ChatGPT or custom GPTs to teams and wanting it done securely, consistently and with real adoption — from SMEs to enterprises.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('Should we use Claude or ChatGPT?','It depends on your use cases, data-safety needs and existing tools — the models have different strengths, and many organisations use more than one. We assess your needs and recommend the right model or mix, then deploy and configure it, rather than pushing a single vendor.'),array('What is a custom GPT?','A custom GPT is a tailored AI assistant configured for a specific purpose and grounded in your own instructions and data — for example, a support assistant that knows your policies, or a research assistant for your team. We design and build custom GPTs and assistants as part of LLM deployment.'),array('How do you keep company data safe with LLMs?','We set clear guardrails: which data can be used, appropriate enterprise licences and settings, access controls, and staff guidance — aligned with your governance and GDPR obligations. This prevents the risk of employees pasting sensitive data into unmanaged personal accounts. See AI governance.'),array('Isn\'t it enough to just buy licences?','Licences alone rarely deliver value — adoption and safety do. Without configuration, custom assistants, guardrails and training, usage stays low and risk stays high. Managed deployment is what turns the spend into consistent, safe productivity.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is LLM deployment?','html'=>'<p>LLM deployment is the process of introducing large language models into a business so teams can use them securely and effectively. It covers choosing the right models and licences, configuring them, building custom GPTs or assistants grounded in your own knowledge, setting data and safety guardrails, and training staff. The goal is safe, widespread, productive use — not scattered, risky personal accounts.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Model &amp; licence selection</h3>
<p>The right LLMs (Claude, ChatGPT and others) and licences for your needs.</p>
<h3>Custom GPTs &amp; assistants</h3>
<p>Assistants built on your data and tone of voice for real workflows.</p>
<h3>Guardrails &amp; data safety</h3>
<p>Controls over what data goes where, aligned with your <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">governance</a>.</p>
<h3>Rollout &amp; training</h3>
<p>Structured rollout with hands-on <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-training/">training</a> so adoption sticks.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Assess</strong> use cases, licences and data-safety needs.</li><li><strong>Configure</strong> models and build custom GPTs/assistants.</li><li><strong>Guardrail</strong> — set data and safety controls.</li><li><strong>Roll out</strong> across teams.</li><li><strong>Train &amp; embed</strong> for lasting adoption.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>LLMs live across your teams, used safely and well.</li><li>Custom assistants grounded in your own knowledge.</li><li>Data risk controlled, not left to chance.</li><li>Measurable productivity, not shelfware.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Organisations rolling out Claude, ChatGPT or custom GPTs to teams and wanting it done securely, consistently and with real adoption — from SMEs to enterprises.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/london/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Alugence is an AI consultancy working with London businesses to adopt AI and turn it into working systems. From strategy and readiness to automation and custom development, we help London firms across finance, professional services, retail and more capture value from AI — with senior consultants and measurable outcomes.</p>',
			'def' => '',
			'cards' => array(),
			'steps' => array(),
			'outcomes' => '',
			'who' => '',
			'faqs' => array(array('Do you meet clients in London?','Yes. We work with London clients both on-site and remotely, and combine local responsiveness with a full UK-wide AI practice. Book a discovery call to arrange an initial conversation.'),array('What types of London businesses do you work with?','We work across London\'s core sectors — financial and professional services, retail and e-commerce, healthcare, property and marketing — tailoring AI use cases to each. See our industries pages for sector-specific examples.'),array('How do we start?','Most London clients begin with an AI Readiness Assessment or a two-week AI Readiness Sprint: a scored use-case shortlist and a costed plan. Book a call to scope it.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'AI consulting for London businesses','html'=>'<p>London\'s mix of financial services, professional services, tech and retail makes it one of the densest markets for AI opportunity — and competition. We help London organisations move from AI curiosity to AI advantage: prioritising the right use cases, building automation and agents, and embedding AI safely under UK and EU rules.</p>'),array('h'=>'What we do','html'=>'<ul><li><strong>AI strategy &amp; roadmaps</strong> — a clear, costed plan (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-strategy/">AI strategy</a>).</li><li><strong>AI automation &amp; agents</strong> — remove manual work (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-automation/">AI automation</a>).</li><li><strong>Custom AI development</strong> — bespoke solutions (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-development/">AI development</a>).</li><li><strong>Governance &amp; compliance</strong> — safe deployment (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-governance/">AI governance</a>).</li><li><strong>Training &amp; enablement</strong> — adoption that sticks (<a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-training/">AI training</a>).</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Local expertise, national reach','html'=>'<p>We\'re a UK consultancy serving London clients on-site and remotely, and businesses across the UK and US. You get the responsiveness of a local partner with the depth of a full AI practice.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/mlops/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>MLOps is the practice of deploying, monitoring and maintaining machine learning models in production reliably — the operational backbone that keeps AI working after launch. Alugence builds MLOps pipelines and AI infrastructure so your models deploy smoothly, stay accurate, scale on demand, and don\'t blow your budget.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>MLOps (machine learning operations) is a set of practices for putting ML models into production and keeping them running well. It brings software engineering discipline — version control, CI/CD, automated testing, monitoring — to machine learning, so models can be deployed, updated, observed and rolled back reliably. Without MLOps, models decay silently and break in ways nobody notices until it\'s costly.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Deployment pipelines','body'=>'<p>Automated, repeatable model deployment (CI/CD for AI).</p>'),array('title'=>'Monitoring & observability','body'=>'<p>Tracking performance, drift and errors in production.</p>'),array('title'=>'Scaling & cost control','body'=>'<p>Infrastructure that scales with demand and controls spend.</p>'),array('title'=>'Retraining & versioning','body'=>'<p>Processes to update and roll back models safely.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Assess','desc'=>'your models and current infrastructure.'),array('name'=>'Design','desc'=>'the deployment and monitoring architecture.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'pipelines and observability.'),array('name'=>'Deploy','desc'=>'with scaling and cost controls.'),array('name'=>'Operate','desc'=>'— monitoring, retraining and support.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Reliable model deployment and updates.</li><li>Early warning of model drift and failures.</li><li>Infrastructure that scales without runaway costs.</li><li>Engineering discipline around your AI.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Technical and enterprise teams running (or planning) machine learning in production who need it to be dependable, observable and cost-efficient. Pairs with <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-development/">custom AI development</a> and <a href="/ai-consultancy/enterprise-ai/">enterprise AI</a>.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is MLOps and why does it matter?','MLOps is the practice of deploying, monitoring and maintaining machine learning models in production reliably. It matters because models degrade over time and fail in subtle ways; MLOps provides the pipelines, monitoring and version control to catch problems early and keep AI dependable at scale.'),array('How is MLOps different from DevOps?','MLOps extends DevOps principles to machine learning, adding concerns DevOps doesn\'t cover — data and model versioning, model drift monitoring, retraining pipelines, and evaluating model quality, not just code. The goal is the same reliability DevOps brings to software, applied to the messier lifecycle of ML.'),array('What is model drift?','Model drift is the gradual decline in a model\'s accuracy as the real world changes and no longer matches its training data. MLOps monitoring detects drift early — through performance and data checks — so models can be retrained before poor predictions cause harm.'),array('Do we need MLOps if we only have a few models?','Even a few production models benefit from basic MLOps — reliable deployment, monitoring and a way to update safely. The investment scales with your needs; we right-size the infrastructure so it fits the number and criticality of your models.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is MLOps?','html'=>'<p>MLOps (machine learning operations) is a set of practices for putting ML models into production and keeping them running well. It brings software engineering discipline — version control, CI/CD, automated testing, monitoring — to machine learning, so models can be deployed, updated, observed and rolled back reliably. Without MLOps, models decay silently and break in ways nobody notices until it\'s costly.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Deployment pipelines</h3>
<p>Automated, repeatable model deployment (CI/CD for AI).</p>
<h3>Monitoring &amp; observability</h3>
<p>Tracking performance, drift and errors in production.</p>
<h3>Scaling &amp; cost control</h3>
<p>Infrastructure that scales with demand and controls spend.</p>
<h3>Retraining &amp; versioning</h3>
<p>Processes to update and roll back models safely.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Assess</strong> your models and current infrastructure.</li><li><strong>Design</strong> the deployment and monitoring architecture.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> pipelines and observability.</li><li><strong>Deploy</strong> with scaling and cost controls.</li><li><strong>Operate</strong> — monitoring, retraining and support.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Reliable model deployment and updates.</li><li>Early warning of model drift and failures.</li><li>Infrastructure that scales without runaway costs.</li><li>Engineering discipline around your AI.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Technical and enterprise teams running (or planning) machine learning in production who need it to be dependable, observable and cost-efficient. Pairs with <a href="/ai-consultancy/ai-development/">custom AI development</a> and <a href="/ai-consultancy/enterprise-ai/">enterprise AI</a>.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/predictive-analytics/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Predictive analytics uses machine learning and statistical models to turn your historical data into forecasts and better decisions — what\'s likely to happen, and what to do about it. Alugence\'s data science consulting builds and deploys predictive models on your data, from demand forecasting to churn and risk, and takes them from prototype to production.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>Predictive analytics is the use of data, machine learning and statistical models to forecast future outcomes from historical patterns. It answers questions like which customers are likely to churn, how much demand to expect, or which cases carry the most risk — turning data you already hold into decisions you can act on.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Use-case definition','body'=>'<p>Finding the predictions that would change decisions.</p>'),array('title'=>'Data preparation','body'=>'<p>Getting your data ready for modelling (<a href="/ai-consultancy/data-strategy/">data strategy</a>).</p>'),array('title'=>'Model development','body'=>'<p>Building and evaluating ML models on your data.</p>'),array('title'=>'Deployment','body'=>'<p>Putting models into production (<a href="/ai-consultancy/mlops/">MLOps</a>) and into workflows.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Define','desc'=>'the decision the prediction will improve.'),array('name'=>'Prepare','desc'=>'and validate the data.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'and evaluate the model.'),array('name'=>'Deploy','desc'=>'into production and workflows.'),array('name'=>'Monitor','desc'=>'and improve accuracy over time.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Forecasts that improve planning and decisions.</li><li>Early warning on churn, demand, risk or maintenance.</li><li>Models embedded in real workflows, not just reports.</li><li>Measurable uplift where predictions drive action.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Data-rich businesses — retail, manufacturing, logistics, finance — that want to move from hindsight reporting to forward-looking prediction and act on it.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is the difference between predictive analytics and AI?','Predictive analytics is a branch of AI focused on forecasting outcomes from data using machine learning and statistics. AI is the broader field — including automation, language and vision. Predictive analytics is specifically about turning historical data into reliable predictions that guide decisions.'),array('What can predictive analytics be used for?','Common uses include demand and sales forecasting, customer churn prediction, predictive maintenance, fraud and risk scoring, inventory optimisation and lead scoring. We start from the decision you want to improve, then build the model that supports it.'),array('What is machine learning consulting?','Machine learning consulting is expert help designing, building, evaluating and deploying ML models — selecting the right approach, preparing data, and putting models into production. It\'s how predictive analytics gets delivered reliably rather than staying a one-off experiment.'),array('Do we have enough data for predictive analytics?','Often yes — many businesses hold more usable data than they realise. We assess your data early and are honest about what\'s feasible; where data is thin, we advise what to collect or how to start with simpler models and improve over time.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is predictive analytics?','html'=>'<p>Predictive analytics is the use of data, machine learning and statistical models to forecast future outcomes from historical patterns. It answers questions like which customers are likely to churn, how much demand to expect, or which cases carry the most risk — turning data you already hold into decisions you can act on.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Use-case definition</h3>
<p>Finding the predictions that would change decisions.</p>
<h3>Data preparation</h3>
<p>Getting your data ready for modelling (<a href="/ai-consultancy/data-strategy/">data strategy</a>).</p>
<h3>Model development</h3>
<p>Building and evaluating ML models on your data.</p>
<h3>Deployment</h3>
<p>Putting models into production (<a href="/ai-consultancy/mlops/">MLOps</a>) and into workflows.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Define</strong> the decision the prediction will improve.</li><li><strong>Prepare</strong> and validate the data.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> and evaluate the model.</li><li><strong>Deploy</strong> into production and workflows.</li><li><strong>Monitor</strong> and improve accuracy over time.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Forecasts that improve planning and decisions.</li><li>Early warning on churn, demand, risk or maintenance.</li><li>Models embedded in real workflows, not just reports.</li><li>Measurable uplift where predictions drive action.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Data-rich businesses — retail, manufacturing, logistics, finance — that want to move from hindsight reporting to forward-looking prediction and act on it.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/small-business/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI consulting for small businesses is practical, affordable help to adopt AI without a big budget or a technical team. Alugence gives small businesses a no-jargon path to AI: we find the tasks worth automating, set up the right tools, and get your team using them — so you save time and compete with much larger firms.</p>',
			'def' => '',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'A focused starting point','body'=>'<p>We find one or two high-value automations you can put live quickly.</p>'),array('title'=>'Right-sized tools','body'=>'<p>Practical, affordable tools set up for your business — no over-engineering.</p>'),array('title'=>'Hands-on setup','body'=>'<p>We configure and connect everything, so you\'re not left with a manual.</p>'),array('title'=>'Training','body'=>'<p>Simple, practical training so your team is confident.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Quick review','desc'=>'of your tasks and tools.'),array('name'=>'Pick','desc'=>'one or two high-value quick wins.'),array('name'=>'Set up','desc'=>'the tools and automations.'),array('name'=>'Train','desc'=>'your team.'),array('name'=>'Review','desc'=>'results and plan the next step.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Hours of admin saved each week.</li><li>24/7 customer response without extra staff.</li><li>Affordable, jargon-free AI adoption.</li><li>A clear next step once the first win lands.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Owner-managed and small businesses — trades, clinics, agencies, shops, professional practices — that want the benefits of AI without enterprise complexity or cost.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('Is AI consulting affordable for a small business?','Yes. We deliberately right-size engagements for small businesses — starting with one or two quick wins rather than a large programme — so the cost is proportionate and pays back quickly. Estimate your potential saving with the AI ROI Calculator.'),array('What can a small business actually use AI for?','Common quick wins include automating admin and data entry, handling customer enquiries with an AI chatbot, drafting content and quotes, summarising documents, and booking appointments. We pick the ones with the fastest payback for your business.'),array('Do I need technical skills or staff?','No. We handle setup, integration and configuration, and train your team in plain English. The goal is tools your people can use confidently, not a system that needs an IT department.'),array('How quickly will we see results?','Small-business quick wins can often go live within a few weeks and start saving time immediately. We begin with the highest-value, lowest-effort automation so you see a return fast, then build from there.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'Why AI matters for small businesses','html'=>'<p>AI levels the playing field. A small team can now automate admin, answer customer enquiries around the clock, and produce work that used to need extra headcount. The barrier isn\'t cost anymore — it\'s knowing where to start. That\'s what we fix.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>A focused starting point</h3>
<p>We find one or two high-value automations you can put live quickly.</p>
<h3>Right-sized tools</h3>
<p>Practical, affordable tools set up for your business — no over-engineering.</p>
<h3>Hands-on setup</h3>
<p>We configure and connect everything, so you\'re not left with a manual.</p>
<h3>Training</h3>
<p>Simple, practical training so your team is confident.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Quick review</strong> of your tasks and tools.</li><li><strong>Pick</strong> one or two high-value quick wins.</li><li><strong>Set up</strong> the tools and automations.</li><li><strong>Train</strong> your team.</li><li><strong>Review</strong> results and plan the next step.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Hours of admin saved each week.</li><li>24/7 customer response without extra staff.</li><li>Affordable, jargon-free AI adoption.</li><li>A clear next step once the first win lands.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Owner-managed and small businesses — trades, clinics, agencies, shops, professional practices — that want the benefits of AI without enterprise complexity or cost.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-consultancy/voice-ai/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Voice AI is technology that lets an AI agent speak and listen on the phone, handling real conversations with your customers. Alugence builds voice AI agents that answer calls, qualify leads, book appointments and handle routine enquiries — naturally, on-brand and available 24/7 — so no call goes unanswered and your team is freed from the phones.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>Voice AI is conversational AI that operates through speech rather than text. A voice AI agent understands what a caller says, responds in a natural voice, and can take actions like booking an appointment or capturing details. Built on modern speech and language models, today\'s voice agents sound natural and handle interruptions and follow-ups far better than old phone menus.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Custom voice agent','body'=>'<p>An agent scripted around your calls, grounded in your information.</p>'),array('title'=>'Telephony integration','body'=>'<p>Connection to your phone system and numbers.</p>'),array('title'=>'Actions & booking','body'=>'<p>Integration with booking, CRM and helpdesk so calls get resolved.</p>'),array('title'=>'Escalation','body'=>'<p>Smart handoff to a human when needed.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Map','desc'=>'your call types and desired outcomes.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'the voice agent and its guardrails.'),array('name'=>'Integrate','desc'=>'with telephony and systems.'),array('name'=>'Test','desc'=>'with real call scenarios.'),array('name'=>'Launch & refine','desc'=>'using call data.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Every call answered, day or night.</li><li>Leads qualified and appointments booked automatically.</li><li>Lower call-handling costs.</li><li>A consistent, on-brand phone experience.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Businesses with high call volumes or missed out-of-hours calls — clinics, property, home services, retail — that want to capture every enquiry without staffing the phones around the clock.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What can a voice AI agent do?','A voice AI agent can answer calls, understand what a caller needs, answer common questions, qualify leads, book or reschedule appointments, capture details into your CRM, and escalate to a human when appropriate — all in a natural voice, 24/7.'),array('Does voice AI sound robotic?','Modern voice AI, built on current speech models, sounds natural and conversational — handling interruptions, follow-ups and varied phrasing far better than legacy phone menus. We tune tone and scripting to your brand so it feels like a helpful member of your team.'),array('Can it integrate with our phone system?','Yes. We integrate voice AI with your telephony and business numbers, and connect it to your booking system, CRM or helpdesk so it can actually resolve calls, not just talk. Complex or sensitive calls are handed off to a person.'),array('Is voice AI suitable for my business?','It\'s a strong fit for any business that takes routine calls — bookings, enquiries, qualification — especially where calls are missed out of hours. We assess your call types first and only recommend it where it will genuinely improve service and capture more business.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is voice AI?','html'=>'<p>Voice AI is conversational AI that operates through speech rather than text. A voice AI agent understands what a caller says, responds in a natural voice, and can take actions like booking an appointment or capturing details. Built on modern speech and language models, today\'s voice agents sound natural and handle interruptions and follow-ups far better than old phone menus.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Custom voice agent</h3>
<p>An agent scripted around your calls, grounded in your information.</p>
<h3>Telephony integration</h3>
<p>Connection to your phone system and numbers.</p>
<h3>Actions &amp; booking</h3>
<p>Integration with booking, CRM and helpdesk so calls get resolved.</p>
<h3>Escalation</h3>
<p>Smart handoff to a human when needed.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Map</strong> your call types and desired outcomes.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> the voice agent and its guardrails.</li><li><strong>Integrate</strong> with telephony and systems.</li><li><strong>Test</strong> with real call scenarios.</li><li><strong>Launch &amp; refine</strong> using call data.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Every call answered, day or night.</li><li>Leads qualified and appointments booked automatically.</li><li>Lower call-handling costs.</li><li>A consistent, on-brand phone experience.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Businesses with high call volumes or missed out-of-hours calls — clinics, property, home services, retail — that want to capture every enquiry without staffing the phones around the clock.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-search/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI search optimisation is the practice of making your brand visible and citable in AI-generated answers — from ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity to Google AI Overviews. Alugence is an AI search consultancy that gets you found by AI: through generative engine optimisation (GEO), answer engine optimisation (AEO) and AI SEO, we turn AI answers into traffic, trust and leads.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI search optimisation is the discipline of getting a brand mentioned, cited and recommended in the answers that AI engines generate. When someone asks ChatGPT or Google\'s AI Overview for a recommendation, AI search optimisation is what makes <em>your</em> business the answer. It combines GEO, AEO and AI SEO — the modern successors to classic search optimisation.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'','body'=>'<p><a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO)</a> — get cited in generative AI answers.</p>'),array('title'=>'','body'=>'<p><a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">Answer Engine Optimisation (AEO)</a> — win answer-engine and AI Overview placements.</p>'),array('title'=>'','body'=>'<p><a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">AI Search Visibility Tracking &amp; Audits</a> — measure and grow your presence across AI engines.</p>'),array('title'=>'','body'=>'<p><a href="/ai-search/llm-optimisation/">LLM &amp; ChatGPT Optimisation</a> — be the source AI models quote.</p>'),array('title'=>'','body'=>'<p><a href="/ai-search/ai-seo/">AI SEO</a> — bridge classic SEO and AI search.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(),
			'outcomes' => '',
			'who' => '<p>Most clients start with an <strong>AI Visibility Audit</strong>: a baseline of where you appear across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews, a GEO/AEO gap analysis, and a prioritised action plan. From there we run a <strong>GEO/AEO Sprint</strong> to implement the fixes, then an ongoing <strong>retainer</strong> to grow and track your AI share of voice. See <a href="/pricing/">pricing</a>.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is AI search optimisation?','AI search optimisation is the practice of making a brand visible and citable in AI-generated answers from engines like ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews. It combines generative engine optimisation (GEO), answer engine optimisation (AEO) and AI SEO so your content becomes the answer these systems give.'),array('How is AI search different from SEO?','Traditional SEO aims to rank web pages in a list of links; AI search optimisation aims to get your brand cited inside a generated answer, where there may be no list at all. The tactics overlap — quality content, structure and authority — but AI search adds entity clarity, answer-first content, schema and citation building. See AEO vs GEO vs SEO.'),array('Which AI engines do you optimise for?','ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews and AI Mode, Gemini, Perplexity and Microsoft Copilot. Our audit shows where you currently appear across these engines, and we prioritise the ones that matter most for your audience.'),array('How do you measure AI search visibility?','We track how often your brand is mentioned and cited across AI engines for the prompts your customers use, your share of voice versus competitors, and how that changes over time. See AI Search Visibility Tracking.'),array('How long until we see results in AI search?','Some fixes surface within weeks as engines re-crawl and update; building durable citation strength and share of voice typically takes a few months of sustained work. The upside is that many AI-search terms are still low-competition, so gains can come faster than in mature SEO markets.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI search optimisation?','html'=>'<p>AI search optimisation is the discipline of getting a brand mentioned, cited and recommended in the answers that AI engines generate. When someone asks ChatGPT or Google\'s AI Overview for a recommendation, AI search optimisation is what makes <em>your</em> business the answer. It combines GEO, AEO and AI SEO — the modern successors to classic search optimisation.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our AI search services','html'=>'<ul><li><a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO)</a> — get cited in generative AI answers.</li><li><a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">Answer Engine Optimisation (AEO)</a> — win answer-engine and AI Overview placements.</li><li><a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">AI Search Visibility Tracking &amp; Audits</a> — measure and grow your presence across AI engines.</li><li><a href="/ai-search/llm-optimisation/">LLM &amp; ChatGPT Optimisation</a> — be the source AI models quote.</li><li><a href="/ai-search/ai-seo/">AI SEO</a> — bridge classic SEO and AI search.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Why AI search matters now','html'=>'<p>Customers increasingly get answers from AI without ever clicking a blue link. If AI engines don\'t know, trust and cite your brand, you\'re invisible at the exact moment of decision. AI search is still an open field with low competition on many terms — which makes now the moment to claim your position.</p>'),array('h'=>'How we work','html'=>'<p>Most clients start with an <strong>AI Visibility Audit</strong>: a baseline of where you appear across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews, a GEO/AEO gap analysis, and a prioritised action plan. From there we run a <strong>GEO/AEO Sprint</strong> to implement the fixes, then an ongoing <strong>retainer</strong> to grow and track your AI share of voice. See <a href="/pricing/">pricing</a>.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI search visibility is how often — and how favourably — your brand appears in the answers that AI engines give. Alugence measures your AI search visibility across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Copilot, benchmarks you against competitors, and gives you a prioritised plan to grow your presence. You can\'t improve what you can\'t see; we make it visible.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI search visibility is a measure of a brand\'s presence in AI-generated answers — how frequently it\'s mentioned, cited or recommended when people ask AI engines relevant questions, and how it compares to competitors (its "share of voice"). It\'s the AI-era equivalent of search rankings, and the baseline metric for any GEO or AEO programme.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Visibility audit & baseline','body'=>'<p>Where you appear across major AI engines for your key prompts, today.</p>'),array('title'=>'Competitor benchmark','body'=>'<p>Your share of voice versus rivals — who AI recommends instead of you.</p>'),array('title'=>'Gap analysis','body'=>'<p>Why you\'re missing, and the highest-impact fixes.</p>'),array('title'=>'Ongoing tracking','body'=>'<p>Continuous monitoring so you can see progress and prove ROI.</p>'),array('title'=>'Reporting','body'=>'<p>Clear monthly reporting on mentions, citations and share of voice.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Define','desc'=>'the prompts and questions your customers use.'),array('name'=>'Measure','desc'=>'your presence across AI engines.'),array('name'=>'Benchmark','desc'=>'against competitors.'),array('name'=>'Diagnose','desc'=>'the gaps and priorities.'),array('name'=>'Track','desc'=>'progress on an ongoing basis.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>A clear baseline of your AI search visibility.</li><li>Knowledge of where competitors beat you and why.</li><li>A prioritised plan to close the gaps.</li><li>Ongoing proof of progress and ROI.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Any brand that wants to know — and grow — how it shows up in AI answers. It\'s the natural first step before a <a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a> or <a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">AEO</a> programme.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is AI search visibility?','AI search visibility measures how often and how favourably your brand appears in AI-generated answers across engines like ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Copilot. It includes your mentions, citations and share of voice versus competitors — the core metric for tracking progress in AI search.'),array('How do you track visibility across AI engines?','We run the prompts your customers actually use across the major AI engines and record how often your brand is mentioned and cited, in what context, and how you compare to competitors. We repeat this over time to show trends and prove the impact of optimisation work.'),array('Do I need a tool or a service?','There are AI visibility tools, but the value is in interpretation and action. Alugence provides tracking *and* the expert audit, competitor benchmark and prioritised plan that turn data into results — see our round-up of the best AI search visibility tools for the tooling landscape.'),array('What is share of voice in AI search?','Share of voice in AI search is the proportion of relevant AI answers that mention or cite your brand, compared with competitors. A rising share of voice means AI engines are increasingly choosing you as the answer — the outcome GEO and AEO work aims to grow.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI search visibility?','html'=>'<p>AI search visibility is a measure of a brand\'s presence in AI-generated answers — how frequently it\'s mentioned, cited or recommended when people ask AI engines relevant questions, and how it compares to competitors (its "share of voice"). It\'s the AI-era equivalent of search rankings, and the baseline metric for any GEO or AEO programme.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Visibility audit &amp; baseline</h3>
<p>Where you appear across major AI engines for your key prompts, today.</p>
<h3>Competitor benchmark</h3>
<p>Your share of voice versus rivals — who AI recommends instead of you.</p>
<h3>Gap analysis</h3>
<p>Why you\'re missing, and the highest-impact fixes.</p>
<h3>Ongoing tracking</h3>
<p>Continuous monitoring so you can see progress and prove ROI.</p>
<h3>Reporting</h3>
<p>Clear monthly reporting on mentions, citations and share of voice.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Define</strong> the prompts and questions your customers use.</li><li><strong>Measure</strong> your presence across AI engines.</li><li><strong>Benchmark</strong> against competitors.</li><li><strong>Diagnose</strong> the gaps and priorities.</li><li><strong>Track</strong> progress on an ongoing basis.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>A clear baseline of your AI search visibility.</li><li>Knowledge of where competitors beat you and why.</li><li>A prioritised plan to close the gaps.</li><li>Ongoing proof of progress and ROI.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Any brand that wants to know — and grow — how it shows up in AI answers. It\'s the natural first step before a <a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a> or <a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">AEO</a> programme.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-search/ai-seo-london/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Alugence is an AI SEO consultancy working with London businesses to rank in Google <em>and</em> get cited by AI engines. We modernise your SEO for the age of AI search — improving traditional rankings while growing your visibility across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews.</p>',
			'def' => '',
			'cards' => array(),
			'steps' => array(),
			'outcomes' => '',
			'who' => '',
			'faqs' => array(array('Do you offer AI SEO for London businesses specifically?','Yes. We work with London organisations on both traditional SEO and AI search visibility, tailoring the strategy to London\'s competitive market. We meet clients in London and work remotely across the UK and US.'),array('What does an AI SEO consultant do?','An AI SEO consultant modernises your search strategy for AI: improving Google rankings and technical SEO while optimising your brand and content to be cited in AI answers from ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews. See our main AI SEO page.'),array('How do we get started?','Start with an AI SEO or AI Visibility audit to see where you stand in both traditional and AI search, then a prioritised action plan. Book a consultation to arrange it.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'AI SEO for London businesses','html'=>'<p>London is one of the most competitive search markets anywhere, and AI search is reshaping it fast. We help London brands stay visible on both fronts: winning rankings and featured snippets, and earning the AI citations that increasingly decide who customers find first.</p>'),array('h'=>'What we do','html'=>'<ul><li><strong>AI SEO audit</strong> — traditional and AI search performance (<a href="/ai-search/ai-seo/">AI SEO</a>).</li><li><strong>GEO &amp; AEO</strong> — get cited in AI answers (<a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a>, <a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">AEO</a>).</li><li><strong>AI visibility tracking</strong> — measure your presence (<a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">visibility</a>).</li><li><strong>Content &amp; technical optimisation</strong> — the foundations that still matter.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Local expertise, national reach','html'=>'<p>We work with London clients on-site and remotely, and with businesses across the UK and US. You get responsive, local partnership backed by a full AI search practice.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-search/ai-seo/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>AI SEO is search engine optimisation adapted for a world where AI generates answers — helping you rank in Google <em>and</em> get cited by AI engines like ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity. Alugence\'s AI SEO consultancy bridges classic SEO and AI search, using AI to work smarter and optimising your content for both traditional rankings and AI citations.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>AI SEO has two connected meanings: optimising your content to perform in AI-driven search (AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity), and using AI tools to do SEO faster and smarter. Alugence covers both — modernising your SEO so it wins in AI search, while applying AI to research, content and technical work. It\'s the bridge from traditional SEO to GEO and AEO.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'AI SEO audit','body'=>'<p>How your site performs in both traditional and AI search.</p>'),array('title'=>'Foundations & technical SEO','body'=>'<p>The rankings basics AI search still relies on.</p>'),array('title'=>'AI search optimisation','body'=>'<p>Answer-first content, entity signals and schema for <a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a> and <a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">AEO</a>.</p>'),array('title'=>'AI-assisted content','body'=>'<p>Using AI to scale research and content, with human quality control.</p>'),array('title'=>'Measurement','body'=>'<p>Rankings, AI Overviews presence and AI citations together.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Audit','desc'=>'traditional and AI search performance.'),array('name'=>'Fix','desc'=>'technical and content foundations.'),array('name'=>'Optimise','desc'=>'for AI Overviews and AI citations.'),array('name'=>'Produce','desc'=>'AI-assisted, human-checked content.'),array('name'=>'Measure','desc'=>'rankings and AI visibility together.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Rankings in Google plus citations in AI answers.</li><li>A smooth bridge from classic SEO to AI search.</li><li>Content that serves readers, search engines and AI models.</li><li>One partner and one strategy across both worlds.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Businesses and marketers with existing SEO who don\'t want to be left behind as AI reshapes search — and anyone looking for an AI SEO consultant to modernise their approach.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is AI SEO?','AI SEO means optimising content to perform in AI-driven search — such as Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT and Perplexity — and using AI tools to do SEO more efficiently. It bridges traditional SEO with the newer disciplines of generative engine optimisation (GEO) and answer engine optimisation (AEO).'),array('Is traditional SEO dead?','No — but it\'s changing. Rankings, quality content and technical health still matter, and AI engines often draw on the same signals. What\'s changed is that being cited inside AI answers now matters alongside ranking links. AI SEO evolves your existing SEO rather than replacing it. See AI SEO vs traditional SEO.'),array('Do I need AI SEO or GEO/AEO?','They\'re connected. AI SEO is the broad, bridging discipline; GEO and AEO are the specific practices for generative engines and answer engines within it. Many clients start with AI SEO to modernise the whole approach, then invest deeper in GEO and AEO where it matters most.'),array('Can I work with an AI SEO consultant on a small budget?','Yes. We scope AI SEO to your size and goals — an audit and a focused set of priorities can deliver a lot without a large retainer. Quick-win improvements to structure, entities and answer-first content often move the needle first. See pricing.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is AI SEO?','html'=>'<p>AI SEO has two connected meanings: optimising your content to perform in AI-driven search (AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity), and using AI tools to do SEO faster and smarter. Alugence covers both — modernising your SEO so it wins in AI search, while applying AI to research, content and technical work. It\'s the bridge from traditional SEO to GEO and AEO.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>AI SEO audit</h3>
<p>How your site performs in both traditional and AI search.</p>
<h3>Foundations &amp; technical SEO</h3>
<p>The rankings basics AI search still relies on.</p>
<h3>AI search optimisation</h3>
<p>Answer-first content, entity signals and schema for <a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a> and <a href="/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/">AEO</a>.</p>
<h3>AI-assisted content</h3>
<p>Using AI to scale research and content, with human quality control.</p>
<h3>Measurement</h3>
<p>Rankings, AI Overviews presence and AI citations together.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Audit</strong> traditional and AI search performance.</li><li><strong>Fix</strong> technical and content foundations.</li><li><strong>Optimise</strong> for AI Overviews and AI citations.</li><li><strong>Produce</strong> AI-assisted, human-checked content.</li><li><strong>Measure</strong> rankings and AI visibility together.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Rankings in Google plus citations in AI answers.</li><li>A smooth bridge from classic SEO to AI search.</li><li>Content that serves readers, search engines and AI models.</li><li>One partner and one strategy across both worlds.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Businesses and marketers with existing SEO who don\'t want to be left behind as AI reshapes search — and anyone looking for an AI SEO consultant to modernise their approach.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-search/answer-engine-optimisation/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Answer Engine Optimisation (AEO) is the practice of structuring your content so answer engines — like Google AI Overviews and featured snippets — quote your business as the answer. Alugence\'s AEO services make your content the clean, direct, well-structured source that answer engines prefer to lift, putting you at the top of the answer.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>Answer engine optimisation (AEO) is the practice of optimising content to be selected as the direct answer by answer engines and AI-generated results. It focuses on giving a clear, self-contained answer to a specific question, structured so machines can extract it — through answer-first writing, FAQ formatting, schema and clear headings. AEO is how you win the "position zero" of the AI era.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'AEO audit','body'=>'<p>Which questions you could own, and where you\'re losing them.</p>'),array('title'=>'Answer-first restructuring','body'=>'<p>Rewriting key content to lead with the answer.</p>'),array('title'=>'FAQ & schema','body'=>'<p>FAQ blocks and FAQPage/other schema that make answers explicit.</p>'),array('title'=>'Content structuring','body'=>'<p>Headings, lists and tables engines can extract cleanly.</p>'),array('title'=>'Tracking','body'=>'<p>Monitoring answer placements and AI Overview presence.</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Audit','desc'=>'target questions and current answer placements.'),array('name'=>'Restructure','desc'=>'key content to be answer-first.'),array('name'=>'Add','desc'=>'FAQ blocks and schema.'),array('name'=>'Optimise','desc'=>'headings, lists and tables for extraction.'),array('name'=>'Track','desc'=>'placements and refine.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>More featured snippet and AI Overview placements.</li><li>Your content quoted as the direct answer.</li><li>Higher visibility for high-intent questions.</li><li>A repeatable method for owning new questions.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Businesses whose customers ask clear, answerable questions — and who want to be the source the answer engines cite. Especially valuable alongside <a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a> and <a href="/ai-search/ai-seo/">AI SEO</a>.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is answer engine optimisation (AEO)?','Answer engine optimisation (AEO) is the practice of structuring content so answer engines — like Google AI Overviews and featured snippets — select it as the direct answer to a question. It relies on answer-first writing, FAQ formatting, schema and clear structure that machines can extract cleanly.'),array('What is the difference between AEO and GEO?','AEO focuses on winning direct-answer placements (featured snippets, AI Overviews) by answering specific questions cleanly; GEO focuses on being cited across generative AI answers like ChatGPT and Perplexity. They overlap and reinforce each other — most brands need both. See AEO vs GEO vs SEO.'),array('How do you optimise content for answer engines?','By leading with a concise, self-contained answer to each target question, adding FAQ sections and appropriate schema, and structuring content with clear headings, lists and tables that engines can extract. We also strengthen the topical authority that makes engines trust your answer.'),array('Does AEO help with Google AI Overviews?','Yes. AI Overviews assemble answers from sources they can clearly extract and trust; AEO makes your content exactly that. Answer-first structure, FAQ blocks, schema and authority all increase the chance your content is used in an AI Overview. See our AI Overviews guide.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is answer engine optimisation?','html'=>'<p>Answer engine optimisation (AEO) is the practice of optimising content to be selected as the direct answer by answer engines and AI-generated results. It focuses on giving a clear, self-contained answer to a specific question, structured so machines can extract it — through answer-first writing, FAQ formatting, schema and clear headings. AEO is how you win the "position zero" of the AI era.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>AEO audit</h3>
<p>Which questions you could own, and where you\'re losing them.</p>
<h3>Answer-first restructuring</h3>
<p>Rewriting key content to lead with the answer.</p>
<h3>FAQ &amp; schema</h3>
<p>FAQ blocks and FAQPage/other schema that make answers explicit.</p>
<h3>Content structuring</h3>
<p>Headings, lists and tables engines can extract cleanly.</p>
<h3>Tracking</h3>
<p>Monitoring answer placements and AI Overview presence.</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Audit</strong> target questions and current answer placements.</li><li><strong>Restructure</strong> key content to be answer-first.</li><li><strong>Add</strong> FAQ blocks and schema.</li><li><strong>Optimise</strong> headings, lists and tables for extraction.</li><li><strong>Track</strong> placements and refine.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>More featured snippet and AI Overview placements.</li><li>Your content quoted as the direct answer.</li><li>Higher visibility for high-intent questions.</li><li>A repeatable method for owning new questions.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Businesses whose customers ask clear, answerable questions — and who want to be the source the answer engines cite. Especially valuable alongside <a href="/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/">GEO</a> and <a href="/ai-search/ai-seo/">AI SEO</a>.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-search/generative-engine-optimisation/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO) is the practice of optimising your brand and content to be cited in the answers generated by AI engines like ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity. Alugence\'s GEO services make your business the answer these engines give — earning the mentions and citations that put you in front of customers before they ever reach a website.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>Generative engine optimisation (GEO) is the discipline of increasing a brand\'s presence in the responses produced by generative AI search engines. Where SEO optimises to rank links, GEO optimises to be <em>quoted and cited</em> inside a generated answer. It works by making your brand\'s entity clear, your content easily extractable, and your authority verifiable to the models that assemble answers.</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'GEO audit','body'=>'<p>Where you\'re cited today across generative engines, and the gaps.</p>'),array('title'=>'Entity & authority building','body'=>'<p>Making your brand machine-legible and credible (<a href="/ai-search/llm-optimisation/">LLM optimisation</a>).</p>'),array('title'=>'Content optimisation','body'=>'<p>Answer-first, extractable, well-structured content and schema.</p>'),array('title'=>'Citation building','body'=>'<p>Earning mentions in the sources AI engines draw on.</p>'),array('title'=>'Measurement','body'=>'<p>Tracking citations and share of voice (<a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">visibility tracking</a>).</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Audit','desc'=>'current generative-engine presence.'),array('name'=>'Fix','desc'=>'entity, content and schema foundations.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'citations and authority off-site.'),array('name'=>'Track','desc'=>'citations and share of voice.'),array('name'=>'Iterate','desc'=>'to grow presence over time.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>More citations and mentions in ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity.</li><li>Greater share of voice for your key topics.</li><li>Traffic and trust from AI answers, not just search links.</li><li>A measurable, growing presence in generative search.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Brands that want to be recommended when customers ask AI for options — and marketing teams who can see AI eroding their search traffic and want to get ahead of it.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('What is generative engine optimisation (GEO)?','Generative engine optimisation (GEO) is the practice of optimising a brand and its content to be cited in AI-generated answers from engines like ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity. Unlike SEO, which targets ranked links, GEO targets being quoted inside the answer itself, through entity clarity, extractable content and earned citations.'),array('How is GEO different from SEO?','SEO optimises pages to rank in a list of links; GEO optimises your brand to be cited within a generated answer, where a list may not exist. GEO leans harder on entity consistency, answer-first content, schema and off-site citations. The fundamentals of quality and authority still apply. See our AEO vs GEO vs SEO guide.'),array('How do you get a brand cited by AI?','By making the brand easy to understand and trust for AI models: clear entity data and schema, answer-first content that\'s easy to extract, consistent naming across the web, and citations from sources the models draw on. Our guide to getting cited by AI explains the method we use.'),array('How do you measure GEO results?','We track how often your brand is cited and mentioned across generative engines for your target prompts, and your share of voice against competitors, over time. See AI Search Visibility Tracking.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is generative engine optimisation?','html'=>'<p>Generative engine optimisation (GEO) is the discipline of increasing a brand\'s presence in the responses produced by generative AI search engines. Where SEO optimises to rank links, GEO optimises to be <em>quoted and cited</em> inside a generated answer. It works by making your brand\'s entity clear, your content easily extractable, and your authority verifiable to the models that assemble answers.</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>GEO audit</h3>
<p>Where you\'re cited today across generative engines, and the gaps.</p>
<h3>Entity &amp; authority building</h3>
<p>Making your brand machine-legible and credible (<a href="/ai-search/llm-optimisation/">LLM optimisation</a>).</p>
<h3>Content optimisation</h3>
<p>Answer-first, extractable, well-structured content and schema.</p>
<h3>Citation building</h3>
<p>Earning mentions in the sources AI engines draw on.</p>
<h3>Measurement</h3>
<p>Tracking citations and share of voice (<a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">visibility tracking</a>).</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Audit</strong> current generative-engine presence.</li><li><strong>Fix</strong> entity, content and schema foundations.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> citations and authority off-site.</li><li><strong>Track</strong> citations and share of voice.</li><li><strong>Iterate</strong> to grow presence over time.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>More citations and mentions in ChatGPT, Gemini and Perplexity.</li><li>Greater share of voice for your key topics.</li><li>Traffic and trust from AI answers, not just search links.</li><li>A measurable, growing presence in generative search.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Brands that want to be recommended when customers ask AI for options — and marketing teams who can see AI eroding their search traffic and want to get ahead of it.</p>')),
		),
		'/ai-search/llm-optimisation/' => array(
			'intro' => '<p>LLM optimisation is the practice of making your website and brand easy for large language models — ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Copilot — to understand, trust and cite. Alugence optimises your content, structure and entity signals so AI models quote you as a source, turning the answers they generate into traffic and leads for your business.</p>',
			'def' => '<p>LLM optimisation is the work of structuring a website and its content so large language models can read it, understand what your brand is, and cite it accurately in their answers. Because many AI crawlers don\'t run JavaScript and assemble answers from extractable, authoritative text, LLM optimisation focuses on clean HTML, answer-first content, entity clarity, schema and technical access (like llms.txt and crawler permissions).</p>',
			'cards' => array(array('title'=>'Technical LLM access','body'=>'<p>Server-side rendered content, robots.txt permissions for AI crawlers, and an <a href="/blog/llms-txt-guide/">llms.txt</a> manifest.</p>'),array('title'=>'Entity legibility','body'=>'<p>Consistent brand naming, Organization schema and sameAs signals so models know who you are.</p>'),array('title'=>'Content optimisation','body'=>'<p>Answer-first, quotable, well-structured content models can extract.</p>'),array('title'=>'Citation building','body'=>'<p>Presence in the sources LLMs draw on.</p>'),array('title'=>'Measurement','body'=>'<p>Tracking citations across engines (<a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">visibility tracking</a>).</p>')),
			'steps' => array(array('name'=>'Audit','desc'=>'how LLMs currently see and cite your site.'),array('name'=>'Fix','desc'=>'technical access and entity signals.'),array('name'=>'Optimise','desc'=>'content to be extractable and quotable.'),array('name'=>'Build','desc'=>'citations in trusted sources.'),array('name'=>'Track','desc'=>'mentions and citations over time.')),
			'outcomes' => '<ul><li>Your website cited by ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Copilot.</li><li>Clear, consistent entity understanding by AI models.</li><li>AI referral traffic and leads you can measure.</li><li>A durable presence as models update.</li></ul>',
			'who' => '<p>Businesses that want to be the source AI models quote — and anyone seeing AI referral traffic (from chatgpt.com, perplexity.ai and others) they want to grow.</p>',
			'faqs' => array(array('How do I optimise my website for ChatGPT?','Make your site easy for AI models to read and trust: serve key content in the initial HTML (many AI crawlers don\'t run JavaScript), lead with clear answers, keep your brand entity consistent, add schema, allow AI crawlers in robots.txt, and publish an llms.txt manifest. Then build citations in sources the models draw on. That\'s the core of LLM optimisation.'),array('Why isn\'t my brand showing up in AI answers?','Common reasons are that AI crawlers can\'t read your JavaScript-rendered content, your brand entity is inconsistent or unclear, your content isn\'t structured to be extracted, or you lack citations in trusted sources. An LLM optimisation audit pinpoints which of these is holding you back.'),array('What is llms.txt?','llms.txt is a plain-text file at your site\'s root that gives AI crawlers a curated summary of your brand and key URLs, helping them understand and cite you. It\'s a small but useful signal in LLM optimisation — see our llms.txt guide.'),array('Can you track whether AI is citing us?','Yes. We monitor how often your brand is mentioned and cited across ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Copilot for your target prompts, and track AI referral traffic in your analytics. See AI Search Visibility Tracking.')),
			'sections' => array(array('h'=>'What is LLM optimisation?','html'=>'<p>LLM optimisation is the work of structuring a website and its content so large language models can read it, understand what your brand is, and cite it accurately in their answers. Because many AI crawlers don\'t run JavaScript and assemble answers from extractable, authoritative text, LLM optimisation focuses on clean HTML, answer-first content, entity clarity, schema and technical access (like llms.txt and crawler permissions).</p>'),array('h'=>'What\'s included','html'=>'<h3>Technical LLM access</h3>
<p>Server-side rendered content, robots.txt permissions for AI crawlers, and an <a href="/blog/llms-txt-guide/">llms.txt</a> manifest.</p>
<h3>Entity legibility</h3>
<p>Consistent brand naming, Organization schema and sameAs signals so models know who you are.</p>
<h3>Content optimisation</h3>
<p>Answer-first, quotable, well-structured content models can extract.</p>
<h3>Citation building</h3>
<p>Presence in the sources LLMs draw on.</p>
<h3>Measurement</h3>
<p>Tracking citations across engines (<a href="/ai-search/ai-search-visibility/">visibility tracking</a>).</p>'),array('h'=>'Our process','html'=>'<ol><li><strong>Audit</strong> how LLMs currently see and cite your site.</li><li><strong>Fix</strong> technical access and entity signals.</li><li><strong>Optimise</strong> content to be extractable and quotable.</li><li><strong>Build</strong> citations in trusted sources.</li><li><strong>Track</strong> mentions and citations over time.</li></ol>'),array('h'=>'Outcomes','html'=>'<ul><li>Your website cited by ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Copilot.</li><li>Clear, consistent entity understanding by AI models.</li><li>AI referral traffic and leads you can measure.</li><li>A durable presence as models update.</li></ul>'),array('h'=>'Who this is for','html'=>'<p>Businesses that want to be the source AI models quote — and anyone seeing AI referral traffic (from chatgpt.com, perplexity.ai and others) they want to grow.</p>')),
		),
